{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1793351191,"nonce":"LDI/s0F2ctm3u0MBOQ1SdLoo5Nc=","title":"Complete Ashui HXX element tags and typed component props","message":"Rayzor LSP should complete Ashui HXX tags, attributes and prop expressions while markup is still being edited. Current completion handling in lsp/src/context.rs resolves ordinary visible names and receiver members; lsp/src/server.rs advertises only dot and colon triggers. Macro expansion already provides generated-class hover information, but successful whole-document expansion must not be a prerequisite for completion.\n\nOwnership: Rayzor owns the error-tolerant source context, LSP responses and insertion edits, type queries, caching and cancellation. Ashui owns HXX tag naming/resolution, built-in elements, component prop semantics and special/root attributes. Define a small library-owned metadata/provider interface instead of duplicating Ashui's tables and lowering rules in Rayzor. RayDE should honor the completion capability and edits supplied by the server.\n\nExpected behavior:\n- After an incomplete opening or closing tag, suggest built-ins and visible project components with the correct kebab-case/package spelling. Honor Ashui's import resolution and built-in shadowing rules.\n- Inside an opening tag, offer the resolved Component\u003cProps\u003e fields with types, documentation and optionality, following typedefs and inherited generic substitutions. Include applicable root/layout attributes, events, class/style/ref and supported DSL forms from the provider. Avoid suggesting props already present.\n- Inside a prop expression, preserve normal local/member completion and use the expected prop type for enum values and callback signatures. Show the actual Haxe type rather than macro Expr/ExprOf wrappers.\n- Return useful partial results from cached declarations before imports, macro execution or full indexing complete. Tolerate incomplete tags, braces and quotes; do not rerun the whole build macro for every keystroke.\n- Use precise replacement ranges and snippets without corrupting markup or surrounding Haxe. Register the required triggers with context filtering so ordinary comparisons and strings do not receive tag suggestions.\n- Invalidate metadata by document/dependency generation, project defines, library revision and compiler/cache version; stale results must not replace newer edits.\n\nVerification: portable LSP session fixtures for built-ins, imported and qualified user components, alias/inherited props, enum/callback values, partial indexing, broken markup and cold/warm BLADE restore. Confirm behavior against Ashui component files such as components/haxe/ashui/components/Dialog.hx and a consuming HXX view. This is tracked work, not an implementation in this change.\n\nSource references: ashui/haxe/ashui/ui/Hxx.hx lowerNode, className, lowerComponent, componentProps and setter/inputSetter. Related general completion issue: 78d6ed595b4f73ece45da146f7aedee3ada74e017e52e4c365885fd2bf2108d7. Related expanded-tag hover issue: c07c045946b17db6b713f10010195b5be5451afa3b5e8ed76f07a27468bac713.","files":null}]}